  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or loaded the scene in a browser, so the look, shadows and framing are unchecked.\n\nThe scene is a 240×240 ground plane plus 10,000 instanced objects in three draw calls:\n- **Trees:** 8,000 trunks (`instances.cylinder`) and 8,000 canopies (`instances.cone`).\n- **Rocks:** 2,000 (`instances.sphere`).\n- **Placement:** scattered over a disc of radius 58 from a fixed-seed LCG, so the forest is the same on every load.\n- **Colour:** each canopy and each rock gets its own HSL colour, applied to a white base material.\n- **Light and fog:** one shadow-casting directional light (`lights.directional` with `shadow: true`), a hemisphere light and neutral environment for fill, and `effects.fog` with density 0.0035. I assumed `effects.fog` is exponential. The docs only show a density option.\n- **Camera:** it orbits at radius 105 and height 60, looking at the origin, with fov 45. Each frame `onFrame` calls `app.camera?.setPose` with `cut: true`. I picked those numbers to fit the whole forest in a 640×360 frame without testing it.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` is set from `requestAnimationFrame` after the first `onFrame` call. A second `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()` also sets it, as a fallback.\n\nOpen risk: I didn't confirm that the sun's shadow map covers the full 116-unit forest, so shadows may be coarse or cut off at the edges.\n\n",
